FRE LAUNCH unsigned Windows preview (not a signed updater) — 2026-11-03 Rust instance UI and profile management corrections.
Acceptance and rationale:
- Restore exact original Home/Welcome conditions for Java, but keep standard library accessible for Rust-only profiles.
- Rust/Horizon profiles display through the real InstanceCardView (same as Fabric), route to full profile PageHeader/NavTabs/Files/Worlds/Logs and never enter Java profile backend.
- Rust profile context menu is the actual shared ContextMenu; deletion uses the genuine ConfirmDeleteInstanceModal both on card and profile, and a backend-only validated rust_delete_profile command. Rust Rename uses rust_rename_profile, preserving worlds, rejecting symlinks/path traversal, and serializes against launch to prevent deleting a running world.
- Single Play attempts already-prepared local Minecraft resources and native launch; no fake progress or claim of official Mojang downloads. Requires authenticated account and owned Java Edition assets. Offline local nickname is not ownership verification.
- Test via pinned Vue/TypeScript and 28/28 frontend regressions, preflight GitHub Actions #41623905661 completed SUCCESS. This green result does not prove new Rust commands compile; this release attempt MUST test that and does not publish unreviewed artifacts.
- Full Windows Tauri build, exact pinned MIT engine, Defender scans of all binaries, SHA-256 manifest and clean NSIS install-launch smoke MUST PASS before artifact upload. No signing key is available; do NOT publish a signed release or auto-update.
- Keep old Java profiles, native saves, game resources, updater publicKey and stable v0.5.9 unchanged.
